@Huang-Wei and I were brainstorming a couple of ideas offline:

1. We store the GVK of the component config in the scheduler and its frameworks. Then we use that GVK for building a decoder to get parsing into the internal types during plugin instantiation.
1. in `pkg/scheduler/apis/config/{version}/conversion.go` we parse the in-tree PluginConfig, convert them to the internal types and marshal them back into the `runtime.Unknown`. Then during plugin instantiation we can just use the internal types.
    1. Alternatively, we change `pkg/scheduler/apis/config.PluginConfig.Args` (internal type) from `runtime.Unknown` to `interface{}`. Then as we convert from the versions, we parse and set the pointer to the appropriate type. We still use `runtime.Unknown` if it is out-of-tree plugin. Not sure if there are precedents to this, but it seems reasonable to me given that these are internal types.

@liggitt, WDYT?
